      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-11-21_WidnesExaminer_art0050" n="art0050">
        <head>WIDNES.</head>
        <p>WIDNES.</p>
        <p>On Sunday morning, the Mayor of Widnes (Alderman Samuel Quinn) attended Divine service at St. Mary's Roman Catholic Church, accompanied by his fellow- aldermen and councillors, tkp sth Lancashire Volunteer Artillery, the 2nd LAncashirla Ruyal Engineers, the 2nd Volunteer Battalion South Lancashire Regiment, the pollee:. magistrates, County Chncil .renresentatives. and Corporation officials; General Post Office staff, and the Fire. Brigade. The collection MIS in aid of theWidnes District Nurses' Fund, and realised a good sum towards that laudable object.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-11-21_WidnesExaminer_art0051" n="art0051">
        <head>TRAVELLEICS DRAMATIC SUICIDE</head>
        <p>TRAVELLEICS DRAMATIC SUICIDE</p>
        <p>Standing benoatti• the shadow of a street lamp in Old Trafford late o i Tuesday, Mr. IV. A. Whitworth, a well- known commercial' traveller residing in Johnson-street, raised a revolver to his head and shot himself through the right temple. A cowtable named Flint witnessed the occurrence,and foundon running up to the scene that the bullet had taken effect, and that Whitworth lay dead. The deceased' bad of late- been in financial difficulties.</p>
        <p>Professor Baylis, cf.the London University Colleges was on Wednesday awarded £2.000 damages against the Hon. Stephen Coleridge, hon. secretary of the Anti- Vivisection Society, for libel charging the doctor with unnecessary cruelty itt,npAtating upou a living dog.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-11-21_WidnesExaminer_art0052" n="art0052">
