        <p>Manta.</p>
        <p>Ebe "Ozamtner openes</p>
        <p>and sustained efforts made by various religioug denominations. We have had the Wesleyan Methodist Million Guinea Fund—a colloF. sal under- taking carried out in a manner reflecting the utmost credit on this distinctly middle-class denomination—and various smaller efforts on similar lines by other bodies of Dissenters. The Anglican Churchmen are now having their turn at combined self-sacrifice, the object being the pro- vision of an immense Cathedral for the diocese of Liverpool. Toe aim of our Church friends is a lofty one, and commands the sympathy of all Christians, whether they are Churchmen or Non- conformists. Our English cathedrals are objects of national reverence and pride ; though they belong to the Church of England, we all feel a sense of proud proprietorship in them, and any scheme for their preservation or—as in this case— for the erection of a new structure entirely, claims the sympathy of all believers, irrespective of creed. Like Rome, a cathedral is not built in a day, and the fact is worth noting that only two cathedrals have been erected in England during the last .500 years. The Liverpool Cathedral is to be a magnificent scructure—a lasting monu- ment to the State Church in this part of the country—and we are gratified to see the noble re- sponse which has already been made to the appeal for fundg. Warrington's share was announced, at the meeting on Tuesday, to already total up to £142 103. and there is every probability that the £200,000 required before the work is commenced, will be raised in good time.</p>
